Package: gtxlsx
Type: Package
Title: Write 'gt' and HTML Tables into 'openxlsx2' Workbooks
Version: 0.3.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jan Marvin", "Garbuszus", email = "jan.garbuszus@ruhr-uni-bochum.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Turns a 'gt' table into a range of cells in an 'openxlsx2'
    workbook, keeping the heading, column spanners, row groups, stub,
    summary rows, footnotes and the styling set through 'gt'. Numbers stay
    numbers wherever an Excel number format can reproduce what 'gt' shows.
    A second entry point does the same for a plain HTML table, so output
    from other table packages can be written to a worksheet as well; that
    path needs nothing beyond 'openxlsx2'.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/JanMarvin/gtxlsx
BugReports: https://github.com/JanMarvin/gtxlsx/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 3.6.0)
Imports:
    grDevices,
    openxlsx2 (>= 1.0),
    utils
Suggests:
    gt (>= 0.10.0),
    lt,
    markdown,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
